<section class="row row-even expanded-row">
  <div class="page">
    <div class="center-column">
      <p class="large-text">
        Free and open source web application for <span>issue and task</span> management
      </p>

      <p class="medium-text">
        The backend is
        <a href="https://rubyonrails.org/" target="_blank">Ruby on Rails</a>
        and uses
        <a href="https://docs.ruby-lang.org/en/master/ERB.html" target="_blank">ERB</a>,
        <a href="https://sass-lang.com/" target="_blank">SCSS</a> compiled to CSS, and
        vanilla
        <a href="https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript" target="_blank">JavaScript</a>.
        In addition, it uses
        <a href="https://turbo.hotwired.dev/" target="_blank">Turbo</a> to make HTTP
        requests quicker.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="large-links">
      <a href="https://github.com/dsandstrom/task_roller" target="_blank">
        <div class="logo-wrapper">
          <%= icon("fork-repo") %>
        </div>
        <p>Source Code</p>
      </a>

      <a href="https://production.task-roller.net" target="_blank">
        <div class="logo-wrapper">
          <%= icon("globe") %>
        </div>
        <p>App in Action</p>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="row row-odd expanded-row">
  <div class="page">
    <div class="feature-highlights">
      <div class="feature-highlight">
        <div class="feature-highlight-pair">
          <h3 class="feature-highlight-title">Open Source</h3>
          <p class=feature-highlight-description>
            Code is available on
            <a href="https://github.com/dsandstrom/task_roller" target="_blank">GitHub</a>.
            Bug reports and feature requests are welcome.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="feature-highlight-icon"><%= icon("code") %></span>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-highlight">
        <div class="feature-highlight-pair">
          <h3 class="feature-highlight-title">Customizable Type Tags</h3>
          <p class=feature-highlight-description>
            Editible names and options to provide organization control.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="feature-highlight-icon"><%= icon("options") %></span>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-highlight">
        <div class="feature-highlight-pair">
          <h3 class="feature-highlight-title">User Levels</h3>
          <p class=feature-highlight-description>
            Four levels of user authorization allows separation of duties.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="feature-highlight-icon"><%= icon("person-group") %></span>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-highlight">
        <div class="feature-highlight-pair">
          <h3 class="feature-highlight-title">GitHub Integrations</h3>
          <p class=feature-highlight-description>
            Repo connection to support automatic import of issues and commit message
            callouts to progress App tasks.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="feature-highlight-icon"><%= icon("fork-repo") %></span>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-highlight">
        <div class="feature-highlight-pair">
          <h3 class="feature-highlight-title">Markdown Editors</h3>
          <p class=feature-highlight-description>
            Text entry allows users to utilize HTML tags while being easy and intuitive.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="feature-highlight-icon"><%= icon("quote") %></span>
      </div>

      <div class="feature-highlight">
        <div class="feature-highlight-pair">
          <h3 class="feature-highlight-title">Secure and Fully Tested</h3>
          <p class=feature-highlight-description>
            Uses popular Ruby gems for auth, has a full suite of backend specs, and used in
            utilizes dogfooding.
          </p>
        </div>
        <span class="feature-highlight-icon"><%= icon("ribbon") %></span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p class="center-text">
      <a href="/features" class="button no-margin">View Features</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="row row-even">
  <h2>Deployment</h2>

  <div class="center-column">
    <p>
      The App can be deployed to your own server or to an application platform (PaaS) like
      <a href="https://www.heroku.com/" target="_blank">Heroku</a>. More over, there is a
      <a href="https://docs.docker.com/reference/dockerfile/" target="_blank">Dockerfile</a>
      available to make deployment more agnostic. Instructions on how to deploy
      and initially set up your instance are on
      <a href="https://github.com/dsandstrom/task_roller" target="_blank">GitHub</a> with
      the source code.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>
